  1:Name            D4-SNCP Numeric Coprocessor error and busy logic;
  2:PartNo          105657-001;
  3:Revision        01;
  4:Date            16/5/26;
  5:Designer        Dave Henry;
  6:Company         Breadboarding Labs;
  7:Location        None;
  8:Assembly        None;
  9:Device          g16v8;
 10:
 11:/* 16/05/2026 V1 Initial version converted from PALASM format in COMPAQ design doc         */
 12:/*                                                                                         */
 13:/*******************************************************************************************/
 14:/*                                                                                         */
 15:/*******************************************************************************************/
 16:/*
 17:DESCRIPTION
 18:This PAL is used in the Magnum processor board to handle the error logic for
 19:the numeric coprocessor. It allows a greater measure of compatibility with
 20:the previous products. It sets up the system to generate an interrupt when 
 21:the error signal is recieved. It holds the interrupt until the service
 22:routine does a write to port F0h. It also holds busy out active until the 
 23:interrupt occurs or till the CPU times out from no activity. This is to
 24:prevent any other numeric processor instructions from being executed until 
 25:the error has been recognized. If the no activity timeout occurs, that means
 26:the CPU hung up on the 287 interface due to different design of the 386.
 27:
 28:In this case, the interrupt will have been recieved by the 386.
 29:In addition, the timer chip selects are broken out to the seperate selects by the PAL logic.
 30:
 31:*/
 32:/* Pin Map 
 33:                               ______________
 34:                              |   D4-SNCP    |
 35:                   !TIMCS x---|1           20|---x Vcc                      
 36:                   !XIOWC x---|2           19|---x !BUSYOUT                 
 37:                      XA0 x---|3           18|---x EN_ERR                   
 38:                   !ERROR x---|4           17|---x NC02                     
 39:                  !BUSYIN x---|5           16|---x IRQ13                    
 40:                     TIMO x---|6           15|---x ONESHT                   
 41:                   !NCPIN x---|7           14|---x !TIM1CS                  
 42:                   !NCPCS x---|8           13|---x !TIM2CS                  
 43:                   !RESET x---|9           12|---x RES287                   
 44:                      GND x---|10          11|---x XA3                      
 45:                              |______________|
 46:
 47:*/
 48:
 49:
 50:PIN 1 = !TIMCS ;
 51:PIN 2 = !XIOWC ;
 52:PIN 3 = XA0 ;
 53:PIN 4 = !ERROR ;

